From ef544df513ea3bf9ad7c34d2bca420fcb2fd3a51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:18:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_tristar_charger: Wake the iPad 5 on plug
 event 72

The J71t match data names event 73 (0x49) as the plug event, but the iPad
5 device tree leaves 73 out of the charger's interrupts: it is not a plug
event (it latches every few seconds while the input current nears 2 A,
measured on the iPad 6 with the same D2365, and on the iPad 5 it latched
once at every suspend entry with a cable in). No listed interrupt
matches, so the charger has no plug wake on the iPad 5: a plug or unplug
does not wake it, and an identified charger is never kept across sleep.

Use the D2365's plug event 72, which is in the iPad 5's list. On a J71t
(trace, 2026-11-17) it latched on an unplug, followed by the
disconnect, and again on the replug, followed by the new attachment; the
iPad 6 shows the same. iOS leaves both 72 and 73 unmasked in sleep
(AppleD2365PMU sleep entry, mask constant at 0xfffffff005915af4).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index 608c6fd..2170cb9 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -1652,9 +1652,14 @@ static int tristar_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(tristar_pm_ops, tristar_suspend, tristar_resume);
 
-/* D2365: iOS reads presence from 0x189 (AppleD2365PMUPowerSource). */
+/*
+ * D2365: iOS reads presence from 0x189 (AppleD2365PMUPowerSource). The plug
+ * event is the D2365's 72, as on the iPad 6: event 73 (0x49) also latches
+ * every few seconds while a source is attached, and the iPad 5 device tree
+ * leaves it out of the charger's events for that reason.
+ */
 static const struct tristar_board j71t_board = {
-	.plug_event = 0x49,
+	.plug_event = TRISTAR_EVENT_PLUG,
 	.connected_bit = true,
 };
 
